@page "/examples/connection-mode"

<PageTitle>Connection Mode · Blow</PageTitle>

<ExampleScaffold Title="Connection Mode"
                 Summary="ConnectionMode decides which handles may be joined: Strict, the default, only joins a source to a target, while Loose lets any handle connect to any other - a source to a source, a target to a target. Use Loose for undirected diagrams where a handle is just a connection point.">
    <Toolbar>
        <label>
            Mode
            <select @bind="_mode" @bind:after="ModeChanged">
                <option value="@BlowConnectionMode.Strict">Strict</option>
                <option value="@BlowConnectionMode.Loose">Loose</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="RemoveEdges">Remove edges</button>
        <span class="bb-muted" aria-live="polite">@_status</span>
    </Toolbar>
    <ChildContent>
        <BlowCanvas Nodes="_nodes" Edges="_edges" FitViewOnInit="true" ConnectionMode="_mode"
                    OnConnect="OnConnect" OnConnectEnd="OnConnectEnd">
            <NodeTemplate Context="node">
                <BlowHandle Type="BlowHandleType.Target" Position="BlowPosition.Left" Id="t" Class="cm-target" />
                <div class="cm-node">
                    <strong>@node.Label</strong>
                    <div class="cm-legend"><span>target</span><span>source</span></div>
                </div>
                <BlowHandle Type="BlowHandleType.Source" Position="BlowPosition.Right" Id="s" Class="cm-source" />
            </NodeTemplate>
            <ChildContent>
                <BlowBackground Variant="BlowBackgroundVariant.Dots" Gap="16" />
                <BlowControls />
            </ChildContent>
        </BlowCanvas>
    </ChildContent>
    <TryIt>
        <li>In <strong>Strict</strong> mode, <strong>drag</strong> from Node 1's right-hand (source) handle: only the other nodes' left-hand (target) handles turn green. Release on another node's right-hand handle and nothing is connected; the line beside the toolbar says why.</li>
        <li>Release on a left-hand handle instead to connect. Dragging the other way, from a target to a source, works too: the edge still runs from the source.</li>
        <li>Switch <strong>Mode</strong> to <strong>Loose</strong> and drag from a right-hand handle again: every handle on the other nodes turns green, and a source dropped on a source connects - so does a target on a target.</li>
        <li>Switch back to <strong>Strict</strong>: the edges strict mode would not allow are removed, since this page keeps only what its mode permits. <strong>Remove edges</strong> clears the rest.</li>
    </TryIt>
    <HowItWorks>
        <li><code>ConnectionMode</code> on the canvas is <code>BlowConnectionMode.Strict</code> by default: two handles of the same type are refused with the <code>Rejection</code> <code>SameHandleType</code>, reported by <code>OnConnectEnd</code>.</li>
        <li><code>BlowConnectionMode.Loose</code> drops that rule; the others - no duplicates, no self-connections, your <code>IsValidConnection</code> - still apply.</li>
        <li>The new edge runs from the handle the drag started at when that is a source, and towards it when it is a target, so a target dropped on a target makes the dropped-on node the edge's <code>Source</code>. <code>OnConnect</code> reports the resulting <code>BlowConnection</code>.</li>
        <li>In Loose mode an edge can name a source handle as its <code>TargetHandle</code>; the canvas then looks for the handle among both types to anchor the edge. A strict canvas does not, which is why this page removes such edges in <code>ModeChanged</code> when you switch back.</li>
        <li>The handles' colours come from this page's <code>cm-source</code> and <code>cm-target</code> classes, which set <code>--bit-blow-handle-bg</code>; while a connection is dragged the canvas's green and red take over.</li>
    </HowItWorks>
</ExampleScaffold>

<style>
    .cm-node { padding: 4px 6px; }
    .cm-legend { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; font-size: 10px; color: var(--bit-blow-text-muted); }
    /* Through the handle's own colour token, so the live valid/invalid colours still win while dragging. */
    .cm-source { --bit-blow-handle-bg: #2563eb; }
    .cm-target { --bit-blow-handle-bg: #d97706; }
</style>

@code {
    private List<BlowNode> _nodes = [];
    private List<BlowEdge> _edges = [];
    private BlowConnectionMode _mode = BlowConnectionMode.Strict;
    private string _status = "Drag between the handles.";

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _nodes =
        [
            new BlowNode { Id = "1", Label = "Node 1", Position = new(80, 60) },
            new BlowNode { Id = "2", Label = "Node 2", Position = new(340, 60) },
            new BlowNode { Id = "3", Label = "Node 3", Position = new(80, 200) },
            new BlowNode { Id = "4", Label = "Node 4", Position = new(340, 200) },
        ];
    }

    private void OnConnect(BlowConnection c) =>
        _status = $"Connected Node {c.Source} ({c.SourceHandle}) to Node {c.Target} ({c.TargetHandle}).";

    // Raised after OnConnect for a connection that was made, so only the attempts that failed have anything to add.
    private void OnConnectEnd(BlowConnectEndInfo end)
    {
        if (end.IsValid) return;

        _status = end.Rejection switch
        {
            BlowConnectionRejection.None => "Nothing connected.",
            BlowConnectionRejection.SameHandleType => "Refused: Strict mode only joins a source to a target (SameHandleType).",
            BlowConnectionRejection.Duplicate => "Refused: those two handles are already connected.",
            BlowConnectionRejection.SelfConnection => "Refused: a node cannot connect to itself.",
            var other => $"Refused: {other}.",
        };
    }

    // An edge made in Loose mode may join a source to a source ("s" as its target end) or a target to a target ("t" as
    // its source end). Strict mode would not have allowed it, and would not find that handle to anchor it to.
    private void ModeChanged()
    {
        if (_mode != BlowConnectionMode.Strict)
        {
            _status = "Loose mode: any handle connects to any other.";
            return;
        }

        var removed = _edges.RemoveAll(e => e.SourceHandle == "t" || e.TargetHandle == "s");
        _status = removed == 0
            ? "Strict mode: only a source joins a target."
            : $"Strict mode: removed {removed} edge(s) that joined two handles of the same type.";
    }

    private void RemoveEdges()
    {
        _edges = [];
        _status = "Edges removed.";
    }
}
